  "releaseNotes": "- fixed errors being thrown when indexing the last element of an EsperAudio object as part of a range\n- fixed inverse transform of EsperAudio objects with partially zero pitch crashing\n- fixed pitch shifting potentially crashing when used on unvoiced audio\n- fixed brightness flag potentially causing a crash\n- fixed incorrect normalization of unvoiced part, which could lead to errors during pitch shifting\n- changed pitch detection smoothing implementation to a lowpass filter, fixing several pitch detection errors\n- improved pitch shifting interpolation to improve sound rolloff\n- adjusted tests",
